title: Conductor Workspace Sprint 0-1 complete — embedded terminals with multi-pane
summary: 'Conductor workspace mode fully operational with embedded SwiftTerm terminals. Sprint 0 proved SwiftTerm renders Claude Code correctly (Ink TUI, colors, prompt, status bar). Sprint 1 added TerminalSessionManager (CRUD, max 8, active tracking), NewSessionSheet (recent projects + folder picker), multi-pane support (tested 2 sessions side by side: deus-backend + deus-frontend). Focus ring click detection required NSEvent local monitor on the coordinator (SwiftTerm NSView eats mouse events) + @ObservedObject on TerminalCellView for immediate redraw. Sprints 2-3 remain: Symphony auto-link and polish/window management.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#conductor'
  - '#terminal-session-manager'
  - '#terminal-cell-view'
  - '#terminal-view-representable'
  - '#terminal-session'
  - '#new-session-sheet'
  - '#container-view'
  - '#conductor-environment'
learnings:
  - SwiftTerm's LocalProcessTerminalView eats mouse events — cannot use SwiftUI onTapGesture or NSView subclass override (non-open methods). NSEvent.addLocalMonitorForEvents with bounds check is the correct approach for focus detection.
  - SwiftUI ForEach with static range does not re-evaluate children when external @Published state changes. The fix is @ObservedObject on the child view observing the state source directly, not let _ tricks or .id() modifiers (which destroy the view).
  - Conductor VERSION file must be bumped alongside package.json versions — it feeds the .app bundle Info.plist and shows in the UI header.
